            <td>Head Nurse Station, Bed Monitoring, MEWS Triage, MAR</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>?? Hospital Admin</strong></td>
            <td><code>medicore.admin@gmail.com</code></td>
            <td><code>Admin@2026</code></td>
            <td>Operations, Wards, Admissions, Discharges, Staff &amp; Billing</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>??? Super Admin</strong></td>
            <td><code>medicore.superadmin@gmail.com</code></td>
            <td><code>SuperAdmin@2026</code></td>
            <td>Enterprise Governance, Multi-Hospital Command, Security Audit</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>?? Patient Portal</strong></td>
            <td><code>medicore.patient@gmail.com</code><br><span style="font-size: 8.5pt; color: #64748b;">(or Patient Code: P-10001 / Staff-registered)</span></td>
            <td><code>patient123</code></td>
            <td>Self-service: 3D Anatomy, Vitals, Appointments, Doctor Chat</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<div class="callout">
    <div class="callout-title">Patient Authentication Policy:</div>
    <div>Patients onboarded by hospital staff (in Patient Directory) can log in via either their registered Gmail or auto-generated Patient Code (e.g. <code>P-10023</code>) with initial password <code>patient123</code>. Patients who sign up independently use their registered email and chosen password.</div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 5: CLINICAL ALGORITHMS -->
<h1>5. Clinical Intelligence &amp; Specialized Engines</h1>

<h3>5.1 3D Anatomical Telemetry Engine (Three.js WebGL)</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Real-time 3D rendering of cardiovascular, thoracic, and digestive organ structures.</li>
    <li>Interactive telemetry hotspots reporting blood flow velocity (1.2 m/s), myocardial perfusion (98%), and organ saturation.</li>
    <li>Lightweight WebGL shaders tuned specifically for daylight healthcare aesthetics without high GPU overhead.</li>
</ul>

<h3>5.2 MEWS (Modified Early Warning Score) Engine</h3>
<p>An automated clinical calculation continuously scores inpatient deterioration:</p>
<div class="code-box">
MEWS = Score(Systolic BP) + Score(Heart Rate) + Score(Respiratory Rate) + Score(Temp) + Score(AVPU)
� Score 0-2 : Low Risk (Standard 4-hour monitoring)
� Score 3-4 : Medium Risk (Nurse escalation &amp; doctor review within 30 minutes)
� Score 5+  : Critical Risk (Immediate Rapid Response Team / ICU Code)
</div>

<h3>5.3 Real-time Patient-Doctor Consultation Bridge</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Direct messaging link between Patient Portal and Doctor Clinical Station.</li>
    <li>Fixed-height viewport architecture preventing viewport scrolling disruptions.</li>
    <li>Web Audio API dual-tone chime alerting physicians upon receiving incoming patient messages.</li>
</ul>

